nd regulations\nHealth and safety\nDoctoral School's Newsletter\nSuggestion box\nLogo and corporate image\nContact\nLog in\nIdiomes\nCatal\u00e0\nEspa\u00f1ol\nSearch Site\nAdvanced Search\u2026\nMen\u00fa\nSearch Site\nAdvanced Search\u2026\nHome\nDoctoral programmes\nFuture doctoral candidates\nAccess and admission\nEnrolling your thesis\nGrants\nOpen day\nInduction plan\nProcedures\nHealth and safety\nLibrary resources\nInclusion\nLife in Catalonia\nDoctoral candidates\nAcademic calendar\nEnrolling your thesis\nMonitoring and assessment\nCross-disciplinary training\nMobility\nWork placements\nDoctoral qualifications\nGrants\nProcedures\nCareers advice\nHealth and safety\nLibrary resources\nInclusion\nWelcome Ceremony\nDoctoral Graduation Ceremony\nEuropean Doctoral Day \u2013 May 13\nDoctoral thesis\nDoctoral theses\nThesis supervisors\nThesis examination committee\nResearch integrity\nDeposit and assessment\nInternational Doctorate mention\nIndustrial Doctorate mention\nCotutelle\nThesis in 4 Minutes competition\nEuropean Doctoral Day - Photography contest\nCRUE #HiloTesis Competition\nExtraordinary Doctoral Awards\nDoctoral qualifications\nEquivalence of foreign doctoral qualifications\nLegalization of Spanish documents\nSant Jordi Micro-stories Contest\nTeaching staff\nTraining for teaching and research staff\nMonitoring of doctoral candidates\nCertifications\nGuidelines for thesis supervisors\nPlagiarism detection\nIndustrial doctorates\nIntroduction\nGovernment calls\nThe added value of an industrial doctorate\nEconomic management \ud83d\udd11\nUPC research groups - Smart City\nIndustrial Doctorate Plan 2026 Information Day\nInternationalisation\nMarie Curie Doctoral Networks\nUnite!\nCotutelle\nSchool\nIntroduction\nFunctions\nGoverning and representative bodies\nQuality\nLegislation and regulations\nHealth and safety\nDoctoral School's Newsletter\nSuggestion box\nLogo and corporate image\nContact\nLog in\nCatal\u00e0\nEspa\u00f1ol\nDoctoral School\nHome\nDoctoral candidates\nEnrolling your thesis\nFees\nFees\nhttps://doctorat.upc.edu/en/doctoral-candidates/enrolment/fees\nhttps://doctorat.upc.edu/++theme++genweb6.theme/img/logo.png\nShare:\nFees\nThe fees for doctoral studies at the UPC are set by the Government of Catalonia. (Official Gazette of the Catalan Government, no. 9438 - 20.6.2025, Decree 125/2025, of 17 June, which sets the fees for the provision of academic services at Catalan public universities and the Universitat Oberta de Catalunya for the 2025-2026 academic year).\nFirst enrolment for doctoral studies\nIf you enrol for bridging courses, the fee per ECTS\n\u20ac27.67\nThesis tutorials\n\u20ac401.12\nAdministration of the academic record (per year)\n\u20ac69.80\nLearning support services\n\u20ac70.00\nStudent insurance (compulsory for students aged under 28)\n\u20ac1.12\nVoluntary insurance (optional)\n\u20ac13\nSubsequent enrolments for tutorials\nEnrolment for tutorials is compulsory every academic year and the fees are paid every year. The fees are the same regardless of whether doctoral studies are taken full- or part-time and the date of enrolment.\nThesis tutorials\n\u20ac401.12\nAdministration of the academic record (per year)\n\u20ac69.80\nLearning support services\n\u20ac70.00\nStudent insurance (compulsory for students aged under 28)\n\u20ac1.12\nVoluntary insurance (optional)\n\u20ac13\nEnrolment of the research plan, enrolment of the thesis deposit and issuing of the doctoral degree certificate\nResearch plan (during the first year)\n\u20ac0\nThesis deposit (you must have enrolled for tutorials)\n\u20ac156.87\nDoctoral degree certificate\n\u20ac218.15\nShipment of the doctoral degree certificate (optional)\n\u20ac40 (outside the province of Barcelona and within EU countries)\n\u20ac90 (outside the EU)\nOther fees\nIssuing of academic certificates\n\u20ac27.27\nDiploma of Advanced Studies certificate\n\u20ac78.55\nStudy on the equivalence of foreign doctoral degrees\n\u20ac218.15\nIssuing of the official credential stating the equivalence of the foreign doctoral degree\n\u20ac218.15\nFee estimate\nThe estimate is calculated according to Decree 125/2025, of 17 June, which sets the fees for the provision of academic services at Catalan public universities and the Universitat Oberta de Catalunya for the 2025-2026 academic year.\nFor students in the European Higher Education Area (EHEA), an average duration of four academic years for full-time doctoral studies is taken as a reference. This includes enrolment for tutorials every academic year, for the research plan in the first year and for the thesis deposit in the last year.\nAcademic years\nConcepts\nFee per unit\nUnits\nTotal\n4 academic\nyears\nTutorials\n\u20ac401.12\n4\n\u20ac1,604.48\nAnnual enrollment fees\n\u20ac70.00\n4\n\u20ac280.00\nAcademic record administration fees\n\u20ac69.,80\n4\n\u20ac279.20\nStudent insurance (compulsory for students aged under 28)\n\u20ac1.12\n4\n\u20ac4.48\nResearch plan\n\u20ac0\n1\n\u20ac0\nThesis deposit\n\u20ac156.87\n1\n\u20ac156.87\nIssuing of the doctoral degree certificate\n\u20ac218.15\n1\n\u20ac218.15\nTOTAL\n\u20ac2,543.18\nNavigation\nAcademic calendar\nEnrolling your thesis\nProcedure\nCalendar\nFees\nStudent financial aid\nMonitoring and assessment\nCross-disciplinary training\nMobility\nWork placements\nDoctoral qualifications\nGrants\nProcedures\nCareers advice\nHealth and safety\nLibrary resources\nInclusion\nWelcome Ceremony\nDoctoral Graduation Ceremony\nEuropean Doctoral Day \u2013 May 13\nQuality, (open link in a new window)\ne-secretaria, (open link in a new window)\nPheDra, (open link in a new window)\nDoctoral School's Newsletter\nWhere we are\nGoogle Maps\nContact\nDoctoral School\nCampus Diagonal Nord, Building NXII (Nexus II). C. Jordi Girona, 29 08034 Barcelona\nTel.:\n93 401 61 53\nFax:\n93 401 07 79\nE-mail:\nescola.doctorat@upc.edu\nDirectory UPC\nContact form\nSocial networks list\nBluesky, (open link in a new window)\nLinkedIn, (open l